{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y_safestan_obs`, a deterministic row-major flattening of the original observed `y` array.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added `y_safestan_obs` because the original model scored indexed elements of `y` inside loops, while SafeStan requires each protected variable to be scored exactly once with a plain top-level identifier. The original `y` remains as context data for the lagged history computations in `transformed parameters`, and `y_safestan_obs[(i - 1) * n_trials + t] = y[i, t]`. The likelihood was vectorized as `y_safestan_obs ~ bernoulli_logit(p_safestan_obs)`, where `p_safestan_obs` is the matching row-major flattening of `p`. The prior on `beta` was already SafeStan-compatible.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> n_dogs;
  int<lower=0> n_trials;
  array[n_dogs, n_trials] int<lower=0, upper=1> y;
  array[n_dogs * n_trials] int<lower=0, upper=1> y_safestan_obs;
}
parameters {
  vector[3] beta;
}
transformed parameters {
  matrix[n_dogs, n_trials] n_avoid;
  matrix[n_dogs, n_trials] n_shock;
  matrix[n_dogs, n_trials] p;
  vector[n_dogs * n_trials] p_safestan_obs;

  for (j in 1 : n_dogs) {
    n_avoid[j, 1] = 0;
    n_shock[j, 1] = 0;
    for (t in 2 : n_trials) {
      n_avoid[j, t] = n_avoid[j, t - 1] + 1 - y[j, t - 1];
      n_shock[j, t] = n_shock[j, t - 1] + y[j, t - 1];
    }
    for (t in 1 : n_trials) {
      p[j, t] = beta[1] + beta[2] * n_avoid[j, t] + beta[3] * n_shock[j, t];
      p_safestan_obs[(j - 1) * n_trials + t] = p[j, t];
    }
  }
}
model {
  beta ~ normal(0, 100);
  y_safestan_obs ~ bernoulli_logit(p_safestan_obs);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"n_dogs":1,"n_trials":3,"y":[[1,0,1]],"y_safestan_obs":[1,0,1]}","protected_variables":["y_safestan_obs"]}
